<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUNNER ENTITLEMENTS - NOT WIRED UP BY DEFAULT. READ THIS FIRST.
  ============================================================================

  This file exists for one reason: on iOS 14 and later, sending to a broadcast
  or multicast address requires the entitlement below, and Apple grants it per
  app on request. See:

      https://developer.apple.com/contact/request/networking-multicast

  Apple's wording: "Your app must have this entitlement to send or receive IP
  multicast or broadcast on iOS. This entitlement requires permission from Apple
  before you can use it in your app."

  It is deliberately NOT referenced by CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS in
  Runner.xcodeproj, because a build signed with an entitlement that the
  provisioning profile does not carry **fails at signing time**. Adding it to
  the project before Apple has approved it would break `flutter run` on device
  for no benefit.

  The app does not depend on it. `HostDiscoveryService` probes the LAN with
  plain unicast on iOS (see `_sweepLocalSubnet` in
  lib/services/host_discovery_service.dart), which needs no entitlement at all.
  Broadcast remains the fast path on Android and on the ESP32 firmware.

  Only add this entitlement once BOTH are true:
    1. Apple has granted it for this App ID, and
    2. the provisioning profile in use includes it.
  Then set, for the Runner target in Xcode:
      Code Signing Entitlements = Runner/Runner.entitlements
  ============================================================================
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.multicast</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
